Make libao the default playback device when AUDIODRIVER is unset.

SoX's own ALSA default cannot open a device in a static binary on a
PulseAudio/PipeWire desktop, so playback (`play`, `sox -d` as output) goes
through libao, whose built-in drivers pick pulse, then ALSA, then OSS.
A non-zero `file_count` means this is not `rec`'s input: libao can't record,
so recording still walks the native backends below.

filetype is set directly rather than through try_device(): try_device opens
the handler with a zeroed format (rate 0), and libao's startwrite divides by
the rate (SIGFPE). The real open later uses the true format.

--- a/src/sox.c
+++ b/src/sox.c
@@ -2536,6 +2536,7 @@
 {
   /* Default audio driver type in order of preference: */
   if (!f->filetype) f->filetype = getenv("AUDIODRIVER");
+  if (!f->filetype && file_count) f->filetype = "ao";
   if (!f->filetype) f->filetype = try_device("coreaudio");
   if (!f->filetype) f->filetype = try_device("pulseaudio");
   if (!f->filetype) f->filetype = try_device("alsa");
